  "problem": "Describe the set $S={-6,-5,-4,...,12}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nQ\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-6$ and $12$ (including $-6$ and $12$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,-6\\le x\\le 12}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $-7<x<13.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,-7<x<13}.\n$$",
